# Working style
- Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/PLAN.md` before starting any task.
- Work in small steps: one feature at a time. Propose a short plan before large changes.
- Ask before installing packages, deleting files, or restructuring folders.
- Give Windows PowerShell commands (use `;` not `&&` if chaining).
- Do not invent library functions or API endpoints. If unsure, say "I'm not sure this exists — check the docs" and link the official docs.
- After each change, explain in plain language: what changed, how to run/test it, what could break.
- Tick the matching checkbox in `docs/PLAN.md` when a task is done.
